            <ArticleTitle>Bronchiolitis obliterans: a rare chronic pulmonary complication associated with Stevens-Johnson syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E22-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pulmonary manifestations are well recognized during the acute phase of Stevens-Johnson syndrome but persistent pulmonary sequela is rarely reported. We report two boys with bronchiolitis obliterans following the acute phase of Stevens-Johnson syndrome and discuss the clinical picture and treatment of persistent pulmonary complications with reference to earlier reports.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
